In `fuzz_demangle.cc`:
```cpp
char Buffer[Size + 1];  // VLA (dynamic stack buffer)
std::memcpy(Buffer, Data, Size);
Buffer[Size] = 0;
char demangled[4096];
google::Demangle(Buffer, demangled, Size);
```

The `Demangle` function is called with `out_size = Size`. The `Buffer` is a VLA of size `Size+1`. The issue is a READ overflow on the dynamic stack buffer `Buffer`.

Let me look at `AtLeastNumCharsRemaining`:
```cpp
static bool AtLeastNumCharsRemaining(const char *str, ssize_t n) {
  for (ssize_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    if (str[i] == '\0') {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

This reads `n` characters from `str`. If `n` is larger than the actual buffer size, it reads past the end of the buffer. The buffer is `Buffer[Size+1]` with `Buffer[Size] = 0`. So the valid readable range is `Buffer[0..Size]`.

